    "field": "Paleoceanography",
    "problem": "Poor constraints on soluble atmospheric iron fluxes during past ice ages limit the assessment of iron's role in climate change, as previous methods for estimating solubility from ice cores are unrepresentative of oceanic conditions.",
    "method": "This paper presents a method using novel rapid-filtration and seawater-leaching techniques on sublimated dust from Antarctic ice cores to provide more representative estimates of soluble aerosol iron flux to the Southern Ocean during the Last Glacial Maximum.",
    "task": "The task is to estimate the flux and solubility of aerosol iron delivered to the Southern Ocean during the Last Glacial Maximum, using novel techniques to analyze dust from Antarctic ice cores.",
