        {
            "source_entity_instance": "EPICA Dome C ice core",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "total atmospheric Fe",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Here we present high-resolution fluxes of total and soluble atmospheric Fe, as well as calculated aerosol Fe solubility, from the Last Glacial Maximum (LGM; 21\u201326 kyr before present (BP)) of the EPICA Dome C ice core15,20 from East Antarctica (EDC; 75\u00b006\u2032S 123\u00b021\u2032 E, 3,233 m.a.s.l.; Fig. 1) and from Marine Isotope Stage (MIS) 2-3 (22-52 kyr BP) from an ice core from Berkner Island (79\u00b0 32.9\u2032S 45\u00b0 32.9\u2032 E; Fig. 1).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "EPICA Dome C ice core",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "soluble atmospheric Fe",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Here we present high-resolution fluxes of total and soluble atmospheric Fe, as well as calculated aerosol Fe solubility, from the Last Glacial Maximum (LGM; 21\u201326 kyr before present (BP)) of the EPICA Dome C ice core15,20 from East Antarctica (EDC; 75\u00b006\u2032S 123\u00b021\u2032 E, 3,233 m.a.s.l.; Fig. 1) and from Marine Isotope Stage (MIS) 2-3 (22-52 kyr BP) from an ice core from Berkner Island (79\u00b0 32.9\u2032S 45\u00b0 32.9\u2032 E; Fig. 1).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "EPICA Dome C ice core",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "aerosol Fe solubility",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Aerosol Fe solubility in EDC and Berkner ice cores. Fe solubility in atmospheric dust deposited at Dome C across the LGM had a mean of 10% (n=23) and 17% (n=11) at pH ~5.3 and in seawater, respectively, and a median of 6% at pH ~5.3 (Fig. 2 and Supplementary Data).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Berkner Island ice core",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "aerosol Fe solubility",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "By contrast, mean Fe solubility at Berkner Island, closer to South American dust sources18, was only 3% during 23\u201350 kyr BP (Fig. 2c) and 1\u20135% at the LGM.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
